It is used for integrate SAP CPI with Azure Cloud
using this we can perform various operations Like CRUD

we have different types of storages in Azure
Blob storage (binary files)
Table Storage (Structure storage )
Queue Storage
File  Storage

 We have sender and Receiver adapters in cpi

 we can integrate different types of applications using this adapter like
 Microsoft share point
 Power Bi
 Microsoft office 365 and other microsoft applications
 and sap and non  sap applications

 Do's
 ----
 Do use the AzureStorage adapter for scenarios that require secure, reliable, and scalable data storage
 and exchange between SAP CPI and Azure Storage

 Do use the appropriate type of Azure Storage protocol based on your data type and use case.
 For example, use Blob Service for binary or text data, Queue Service for message queues,
 File Service for file shares, and Table Service for structured data

 Do use the dynamic configuration to override the sender or receiver channel settings at runtime

 Dont's
 ------
 Don't use the AzureStorage adapter for scenarios that require complex data processing or transformation,
 as the adapter only supports basic CRUD operations

 Don't use the AzureStorage adapter for scenarios that require streaming or real-time data exchange,
 as the adapter only supports batch or scheduled data exchange

 Don't use the AzureStorage adapter for scenarios that require data encryption or compression,
 as the adapter does not support these features

 not supports :
 --------------
 -> The adapter does not support the append blob and page blob storage types
 -> The adapter does not support the SAS token authentication method
 -> The adapter does not support the Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 service
 -> The adapter does not support the Azure Storage Emulator service
 -> The adapter does not support the Azure Storage Explorer tool
 -> The adapter does not support Dynamic Blob Reading
 -> The adapter does not support Directory Scanning


